  "notes": "ALU's official 2025 University Catalog (Version 2) publishes course groupings (core, general education, electives) with total credits, semester count and credits per semester, but does not publish a term-by-term course sequence. Semesters below distribute the catalog's required courses evenly across the catalog-stated 5 semesters x 12 credits, with foundational general education first and catalog-stated prerequisites observed (prereq course placed in an earlier semester). Actual term placement is set with an ALU advisor via the Individual Degree Plan.\nALU awards 'units'; the catalog's tuition schedule prices tuition per SEMESTER CREDIT HOUR, so units are treated as semester credits here.\nCore (30 cr): CJS105, CJS100, CJS110, CJS120, CJS130, CJS140, CJS200, CJS223, CJS225, CJS345. General education (18 cr): COM202, ENG160, ENG170, MAT140, HIST160, PSY110. Electives (12 cr): four courses from ACC, BUS, CJS, FIN, LGS, SCI, HIST, POLI, COM. Prerequisite per catalog course descriptions: ENG170 requires ENG160.",
